        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="H2-LHizYDH277eCy7kqv-75" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;autosizeText=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;fontSize=14;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=20;pointerEvents=1;align=left;" value="Why 4 Neurons in Hidden Layer?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Choosing neurons is part SCIENCE, part ART, part EXPERIENCE&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It is called &quot;Hyperparameter Tuning&quot;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our problem:&lt;br&gt;  Inputs  = 5  (Area, Mumbai, Delhi, Bangalore, Garden)&lt;br&gt;  Output  = 1  (Price)&lt;br&gt;  Dataset = 5 houses (very small!)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;General rule of thumb:&lt;br&gt;  Hidden neurons = somewhere between input size and output size&lt;br&gt;  Hidden neurons = (inputs + outputs) / 2 = (5+1)/2 = 3 ≈ 4&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;So 4 is a reasonable starting guess!" vertex="1">
